    {
      "fileName": "griefs-fury.json",
      "id": "S6X3zFOCLVgRY2gd",
      "name": "Grief's Fury",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "S6X3zFOCLVgRY2gd",
        "folder": "lO7eEXPM4mLROj2k",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Grief's Fury",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "reaction"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Your bonded partner gains the dying condition or their dying value would increase.</p><hr /><p>A lost love. A broken spear. Rage burning through a hero-god. When a myth speaks of a wounded partner, the hero-god often rejects the future. Too many find themselves on a battlefield, clutching a body that they swore to protect. In that moment, the wellspring of power ignites.</p>\n<p>Increase the value of your @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Doomed] condition by 1, to a maximum of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Doomed]{Doomed 3}. You gain a +2 status bonus to attack rolls against any creature that attacked or dealt damage to your partner in the last minute. If you reduce a creature to 0 HP that attacked or damaged your partner, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to twice their level. These benefits last until your bonded partner is no longer @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Unconscious] or for 1 minute, whichever duration is shorter.</p>"
          },
          "frequency": {
            "max": 1,
            "per": "day"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 10
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "Hero-God's Bond"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder #218: Titanbane"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "selfEffect": {
            "name": "Effect: Grief's Fury",
            "uuid": "Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect: Grief's Fury"
          },
          "subfeatures": {
            "proficiencies": {},
            "senses": {},
            "suppressedFeatures": []
          },
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "rare",
            "value": [
              "archetype",
              "concentrate",
              "emotion",
              "mental"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 10,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "hero-gods-bond.json",
      "id": "j9TEwIPFOUTZfVn3",
      "name": "Hero-God's Bond",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "j9TEwIPFOUTZfVn3",
        "folder": "lO7eEXPM4mLROj2k",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Hero-God's Bond",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>At times, the myth of a hero-god includes a favored partner or a bonded ally, such as the hero-gods of promises and shield-bearers, Upion and Warrick. When you gain this feat, select an ally. They are your bonded partner. While you and your bonded partner are on the same plane, you and your bonded partner always have the same doomed value (defaulting to the highest value), so when your bonded partner's doomed condition would increase or be set to a specific amount, your doomed value also increases to match (if it is lower than your current doomed value). When either of you are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Dying], the other knows this immediately, as well as the distance and direction to the dying partner's location. When either of you attempts a recovery check, as long as the other is on the same plane, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the check. You can communicate telepathically with your bonded partner as long as you are within 60 feet of each other.</p>\n<p>You can change your bonded partner by spending 1 week of downtime bonding with another ally.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 6
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "Warrior of Legend Dedication"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder #218: Titanbane"
          },
          "rules": [],
